  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Let me summarize the changes made across all three modules.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the formatting options across all three modules while preserving the existing exports and behavior.\n\n### `defaults.mjs`\n- Added `unitLabel: ''` to `DEFAULT_OPTIONS`, giving `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: '' }`.\n- Wrapped it in `Object.freeze(...)` so the defaults can never be mutated.\n\n### `resolver.mjs`\n- `resolveOptions(overrides = undefined)` now returns a **fresh object** (`{ ...DEFAULT_OPTIONS }`) instead of mutating the shared default.\n- `undefined` (or no argument) returns a fresh copy of the defaults.\n- Rejects `null`, non-objects, and arrays with `TypeError`.\n- Rejects unknown keys with `TypeError` (only `precision`, `prefix`, `unitLabel` allowed).\n- Validates `precision` as an integer in `0..4` (`TypeError` for non-integers, `RangeError` for out-of-range).\n- Validates `prefix` and `unitLabel` as strings (`TypeError` otherwise).\n- Only applies fields that are own properties of the override object.\n\n### `formatter.mjs`\n- `formatValue(value, overrides = undefined)` rejects non-finite/non-number values with `TypeError`.\n- Delegates option resolution to `resolveOptions`.\n- Appends `\" \" + unitLabel` only when `unitLabel` is nonempty.\n\n### Behavior verification\n- `formatValue(12.345)` → `\"12.35\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.34, { precision: 1, prefix: '~' })` → `\"~12.3\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.3, { unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"12.30 kg\"` ✓\n- `formatValue(12.3, { precision: 1, prefix: '~', unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"~12.3 kg\"` ✓\n- `resolveOptions({ unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: 'kg' }` ✓\n\nNo mutable state is shared: `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` is frozen, and every `resolveOptions` call returns a new object. The existing `public.test.mjs` expectations are satisfied without modification.",
